if {HasSpoken} == true:
	I don't have anything more to say.
if {HasSpoken} == false:
	I don't have anything more to say.
	Pray tell, what is happening here?
	I’ve opened the old mausoleum, lad. Can you not see?
	Damn. Another body, then.
	Mary! Did you bathe in gin?
	My indulgence is mine business. But I do have questions about yours.
label Questions
- Whose mausoleum is this?
	Who reposes within this tomb?
	Don’t know and don’t care, son. Some Sharps from years gone by. Spoiled rich folk. End up worm food in their stone coffins.
	They don’t burn the bodies?
	No. Got be all right and proper for them Sharps.
	How do you mean?
	Are you blind? They fancy themselves above the rest of us. The law. The way things need to be.
	Most struggle throwing their loved ones it a fiery pit.
	Yet tis a sacrifice we must all make, lest our swarths rise again and damn the rest of us. But the Sharps? Proper burial. Time to grieve. Bastards.
	jump Questions
- What do you know of the death?
	Where did they find this body?
	Near bonny field. Tis all I know.
	Near that farmhouse where the Glintleys reside?
	Aye, lad. Anything else? Work awaits.
	jump Questions
- Tell me about the grave robbers.
	I see damage, groundskeeper. Chunks cleaved off the stone. What  happened?
	There are few  who still come here, let alone those with any respect for them Sharps. No — they come with disdain. Serves them right, ask me.
	Surely you could not condonate such sacrilege?
	Tis not my hand that cast the damag, lad. Even more questions for a busy man?
	jump Questions
- What has happened to this tomb?
	I see there be signs of grave robbers. Any recent activity or incidents?
	Of course. Although those who steal from the dead need it more than the frames that once lay here.
	How pragmatic of you.
	I’ll have none of your sauce, lad. Ask your questions so I can finish my work.
	jump Questions
- I should be going.
set {HasSpoken} = true
